      "writtenOn": "2026-07-02T11:16:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think early exit wouldn\u0027t cover the case where capture started, but packets arrived say after .1s. I\u0027d handle this case after the timeout has expired. get_capture(expected_count\u003d0) is akin to assert_nothing_captured() - and since this is active sniffing case, we cannot really assert that in any other meaningful way than waiting a bit and declaring \"Oh we\u0027ve waited enough to assume no packets are coming\".\n\nI think this simply needs a:\n\n        raise CaptureTimeoutError(\n            \"Captured %d packets, expected %d on %s (timeout %ss)\"\n            % (len(last_pkts), expected_count, name, timeout)\n        )\n        \n\u003d\u003d\u003e\n\n    if 0 \u003d\u003d expected_count:\n        return PacketList()\n\n    raise CaptureTimeoutError(\n        \"Captured %d packets, expected %d on %s (timeout %ss)\"\n        % (len(last_pkts), expected_count, name, timeout)\n    )",
      "parentUuid": "cef8e1c4_f902ea4a",
